.TH WATERFOWL 1
.SH NAME
waterfowl \- Bryant, a bird, and a song
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/waterfowl
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I WaterFowl
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Snd/WaterFowl.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The whole bird is two lines from a point, and it flaps because the far
ends of those lines are driven by a triangle wave on a period of four
tenths of a second.  Its distance is a cawtooth cubed, so it comes in
fast and drifts away slowly, and its size and height follow from that one
number.  The poem \- "To a Waterfowl", by William Cullen Bryant \- scrolls
up on a second cawtooth of period sixty-five seconds, and the song is
Terry Davis's own, three phrases looped.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/waterfowl.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
